+// (1 << 23) | (1 << 24) — HWY_SVE2 | HWY_SVE, the length-agnostic SVE targets.
+//
+// Highway only implements BitsFromMask for the fixed-length SVE targets
+// (arm_sve-inl.h: "required if HWY_MAX_BYTES <= 64, which is true for the
+// fixed-size SVE targets"), because a one-bit-per-lane uint64_t is not
+// well-defined when the vector length is unknown until run time. highway_xml,
+// highway_json and highway_sourcemap all call it unconditionally, so those
+// three fail to compile for the scalable targets. They are attainable on
+// aarch64 Linux whenever the compiler knows SVE and highway has runtime
+// dispatch, which is every clang recent enough to build bun.
+//
+// Disabling them leaves NEON plus HWY_SVE_256 and HWY_SVE2_128, the
+// fixed-length targets that Neoverse V1/V2/N2 select and that do define
+// BitsFromMask - so no SVE hardware loses its SVE path.
+//
+// This has to be the same value in every translation unit that includes
+// highway: HWY_TARGETS is derived from it, and this file disagreeing with the
+// dispatch tables in bun's own objects would misdispatch at run time. Dep
+// builds do not get the global define table, and bun's objects do not get a
+// dep's defines, so the value is repeated in flags.ts - keep the two in step.
+//
+// A number, not a string: DirectBuild.defines emits a string value as a
+// quoted C string literal, which the preprocessor cannot evaluate.
+const HWY_DISABLED_TARGETS = 0x1800000;
+
 export const highway: Dependency = {
